63,3,2,talk,May,,Exactly. And Option C still leaves us with those scary February bills that feel like second rent.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,I suppose a yearly settle is better than a monthly one.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Servas,,Let us choose the path that allows us to live without calculating every flick of a switch.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,Midori,,I'll support whatever reduces the friction between us. Option B seems to balance stability and fairness.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,Minato,,"I'm leaning away from A. Between B and C, B feels more like a plan.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,May,,I vote for B. It smooths out the costs and avoids the huge upfront fee of meters.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,"If B means less monthly work, I can agree to that.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,4,talk,Servas,,I vote for Option B.,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
